> I understand that I am guaranteed 5 wishes
Only if you empty the wand, charge it with blessed charging, empty it
again and wrest the final wish.  Make sure you Engrave (not zap) the
wand to use it until you've charged it.  There's a (very) small chance
that you'll wrest a wish out of it before you've had a chance to
charge it if you zap it when it's at (0:0).

> the first wish should always be for a blessed ?oCharging.
As David has said, 2 blessed scrolls of charging if you don't know how
to write it (have seen and used / #named the scroll before); an
uncursed magic marker if you do.  You can write blessed scrolls (e.g.
enchant weapon, remove curse, taming...) on blessed paper, and cursed
scrolls (e.g. teleport / genocide) on cursed paper if you marker is
uncursed.
I take it from the fact that you've blessed your luckstone that you've
no shortage of holy water.

> What should I wish for after that?
I'd go for speed boots, but check the armoury in the castle first, as
there may be a pair there.  If there's jumping boots there instead, it
may be worth sticking with those, so long as you remember to use them
(I never do, that's why I like speed boots)

Next, given your lack of weapon enchantment, a magic marker seems
worth wishing for if you've gone for charging scrolls first.  Once
you're very fast and are meleeing things with at least +5 on your
Excalibur and katana, most enemies will fall over very quickly for
you.
Also, a ring of levitation seems worth it at this stage.  After that,
I'd say keep the wand, or maybe go for a second marker if you have the
paper to use up the first one completely.

I wouldn't waste a wish on magic gloves, just make sure you grab a
pair of ordinary non-cursed gloves from one of the dead soldiers
probably strewn all around you. If you've piled up a bunch of unihorns
and elven cloaks and boots in a stash somewhere, /oPoly is worth a
wish, I guess.  I like dex gloves, robes and helms of brilliance, but
I wouldn't usually waste wishes on them.

As for artifacts, if you've learned a bunch of really nice combat
spells (magic missile and fireball, say), you might go for the Mirror
or the Sceptre, which give MR and allow you to exchange your cloak for
a robe.  At that stage you're really overpreparing though, and I'd say
just get on with the game instead.

I'd say keep the wishes for when you know what you're short on.  And
get those leather gloves ASAP - it gives you the option of wishing for
chickatrice corpses in a tight corner.

